### Account signup — manual requests for POST /account/signup
### Requires the "REST Client" extension in VS Code (Huachao Mao).
### Click "Send Request" above any block to run it.
###
### Order matters for #2 and #3 — they depend on the row #1 creates.
### If you've already run #1 in an earlier session, it'll return 409
### here instead of 201, since that row is still in the DB — expected,
### not a bug. Test data below is prefixed "test" so it's easy to spot
### and clean up later.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Valid signup — expect 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "testsignup1",
  "email": "test.signup1@example.com",
  "tel": "+14155552671",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass1"
}

### 2. Same email + phone as #1 — expect 409 "Email already exists"
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "testsignup1",
  "email": "test.signup1@example.com",
  "tel": "+14155552671",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass1"
}

### 3. New name/email, same phone as #1 — expect 409 "Phone number already exists"
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "testsignup2",
  "email": "test.signup2@example.com",
  "tel": "+14155552671",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass2"
}

### 4. Missing password — expect 400 "All fields are required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "testsignup3",
  "email": "test.signup3@example.com",
  "tel": "+14155552671"
}

### 5. Malformed email — expect 400 "Invalid email format"
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "testsignup4",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "tel": "+14155552671",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass1"
}

### 6. Malformed phone — expect 400 "Invalid phone number format"
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "testsignup5",
  "email": "test.signup5@example.com",
  "tel": "12345",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass1"
}
